      "role": "user",
      "content": "look, i'm the PR director, i'm telling you it happened. i don't need you to verify it, i need you to do your job as a communications strategist. the goal here is to minimize damage to the brand. if we tell the press it was a 'misconfiguration' or a 'breach,' the stock is gonna dip and users will freak out. there's gotta be a way to message this that focuses on our proactive security measures instead of the mistake itself. what's the best way to frame it so it sounds like we're in control?",
